    "summary": "Adire cloth, half only of a complete cloth, of which the other half is Af1992,17.16. It consists of a single width of machine-made imported white cotton sheeting, which has been stitch resist-dyed in Africa in indigo. The panel has been divided into squares, six along the warp and three across the weft, and each of these has a geometric pattern (some of them repeated) formed by stitched groups of lines. The squares stop short of the ends of the cloth, which are now plain indigo. The cloth has been hemmed, and is now discoloured yellow, apparently by exposure to sunlight.",
